Hi Giancarlo,

Missing values don't pose any problems. The best place to read up on this is the original paper by MacKenzie et al. (2003). In it, they describe how missing values are handled in the likelihood. However, I'm not sure if Ian followed their exact approach when he wrote the colext function. It might be worth comparing estimates from unmarked with estimates from PRESENCE.

Richard

